            <ArticleTitle>Importance of the first two minutes of heart rate recovery after exercise treadmill testing in predicting mortality and the presence of coronary artery disease in men.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>445-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We retrospectively analyzed exercise treadmill and coronary angiographic data of 2,193 men to compare heart rate (HR) recovery with angiographic and mortality data during a follow-up study of 7 +/- 2.7 years. Only the first 2 minutes of HR recovery predicted mortality (p &lt;0.001), and the HR decrease during the second minute of recovery predicted the presence of coronary artery disease (p &lt;0.05).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
